
Last made: 1/19/25
Servings: 6 to 8 servings
Prep Time: 2 hours
Cook Time: 2 hours
Ingredients:
    2 pounds pig trotters
    2 pounds chicken feet
    2 tablespoons vegetable oil
    1 large onion
    12 garlic cloves
    One 3-inch knob ginger
    2 whole leeks
    2 dozen scallions, white parts only (reserve greens and light green parts for garnishing finished soup)
    6 ounces whole mushrooms or mushroom scraps, such as cremini
    1 pound slab pork fatback
    Black peppercorns
    Bay Leaves
    lemon juice to taste
    Salt to taste (roughly 1 tbsp per gallon of stock. it should be slightly under-salted so that you can season your final dish to taste)


Instructions:
1. For a smokey broth, char the onions and ginger in the oil before anything else. Pull them out and set them aside for the veggie pot.
2. Blanch the bones. Put the chicken feet and pig trotters in a pot and cover with water. Rolling boil for 20 minutes. Much of the impurities and gunk comes off the bones and floats in the broth. Strain the bones and rinse off the grey gunk.
3. Salt the bones and put them in the Instant Pot with the black peppercorns and the bay leaves. Cover with water. 120 minutes on high pressure.
4. Veggie stock: put the charred onion and ginger, the garlic, the leeks, the scallion whites, the mushrooms and the pork fatback in a large stock pot. Just cover with water. Simmer 120 minutes.
5. Pull the fatback out of the pot. Put it in a blender with a small amount of the veggie stock and blend until it has a very fine dice. Stir it back into the veggie stock.
6. When the bones are done, let the pressure off and pull the bones out. Combine the bone broth with the veggie stock. Add salt and lemon juice to taste.

